-- title:
--   Line bundle trivial on both components extends [P']-[P] torically
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime, $M\ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p\nmid M$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ is required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under coefficientwise extension of scalars. Further, $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and $j\in K$ is a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function (`hj`). Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), assumed proper.
--
--   *Special fibre data.* $k$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra; $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; $i_1, i_2$ are closed immersions of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$; `hcover` states that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` states that the scheme-theoretic intersection `pullback i₁.1 i₂.1` is reduced, and `hn`, `hn0` give its cardinality as a natural number $n>0$.
--
--   *Sections.* $\varepsilon$ is a section of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ are $k$-sections of $c_1, c_2$; `hε₁` requires that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equals the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   *Representability of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$.* $D$ is a `RelativePic0Designation` for $X$, that is, a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism `D.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section; `hrep` asserts that $D$ represents the relative Picard functor of $(X,\varepsilon)$ cut out by the condition `algEquivZeroCut`, whose predicate is `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero` — so $D$ carries a Poincaré rigidified line bundle satisfying that condition, every such rigidified bundle on a base $T$ is the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along a unique $T$-point of `D.toBase`, and the zero section pulls it back to the unit. `hsm` and `hsep` require `D.toBase` to be smooth and separated. `hreps` is the corresponding representability statement for the base change of $X$ and of $\varepsilon$ to $k$, represented by `D.baseChange k` (the fibre product of `D.toBase` with $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$), and `hPk` identifies its Poincaré bundle with the base change to $k$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection. Likewise $D_1, D_2$ with `hrep₁`, `hrep₂` represent the corresponding functors for $(C_1,\varepsilon_1)$ and $(C_2,\varepsilon_2)$ over $k$. Finally $\nu_2$ is a morphism from the base of `D.baseChange k` to that of $D_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and `hν₂` states that for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of the base of `D.baseChange k`, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification, along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` and `pullback.snd c₂ t`, of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1 i₂.2 t` of the pullback of `hreps.poincare` along $a$.
--
--   *Generic fibre curve model.* $M\eta$ is a `CurveModel` over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), and $e\eta$ is an isomorphism from $M\eta.C$ to $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q})$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`); $A$ and $L$ are algebras over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ compatibly. The chart hypotheses `Mη_chart_nonempty` and `hMηpin` pin this identification down: the preimage under $e\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart is nonempty, and for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), its germ at the generic point, transported through `Mη.ffEquiv`, has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image under $L \to \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ of the expansion of $a$ in $K$. The hypothesis `hgal` is an equivariance statement: for every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $g$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ fixing the image of $L$, and every pair of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$-points $x, x'$ of $M\eta.C$ over the base such that $x'$ followed by $e\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, the place attached to $x'$ by `Mη.pointEquivPlace` is the image of that of $x$ under the action of [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) at $g$.
--
--   *Special fibre group dictionary.* $G$ is a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $J_{0s}$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup `torus` of $J_{0s}$, and a surjective homomorphism $\mathrm{proj} : J_{0s} \to J_I \times J_E$ with kernel `torus`. The bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $J_{0s}$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with the $k$-points of the bases of `D.baseChange k`, $D_1$, $D_2$ respectively; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` state that these bijections are additive in the sense that the Poincaré pullback at a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the Poincaré pullbacks; and `hproj` states, for each $x \in J_{0s}$, that the first component of $\mathrm{proj}(x)$ corresponds under `ptsI` to `pts x` followed by the comparison morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and the second component to `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   *Igusa models of the components.* $w$ is an [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm k M`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), and $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ are curve models over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ and $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he₁`, `he₂`).
--
--   *Generic dictionary and Abel–Jacobi data.* `gpts` is a bijection from [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones), to the points of `D.toBase` over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}) \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and `hgadd` states that it is additive for the relative group law attached to `hrep.some` via `algEquivZeroGroupCut`. Over $L$: `hDL` is the representability statement for the base change of $(X,\varepsilon)$ to $L$ represented by `D.baseChange L`, `hPL` the corresponding base-change identification of Poincaré bundles, and `ajL` an Abel–Jacobi morphism from $X_L$ to the base of `D.baseChange L` with `hajLε` requiring that the base-changed section $\varepsilon_L$ followed by `ajL` is the zero section, and `hajL` requiring that for every field $K'$, every $\operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every such point $x$ of $X_L$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by `ajL` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` at $x$ tensored with the ideal module of that at $\varepsilon_L$ — in classical terms $\mathcal{O}(x)\otimes\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon)^{-1}$. The comparison morphism $kL$ from $X_{\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}}$ to $X_L$ satisfies `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` over the two projections; $\overline{aj}$ is defined by `hajbar` as $e\eta$ followed by $kL$, `ajL` and the first projection, lies over the base by `hajbar_over`; $\overline{\varepsilon}$ is an $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$-point of $M\eta.C$ with `hεbar` identifying it with $\varepsilon$ and `hεbar_aj` saying that it is carried by $\overline{aj}$ to the zero section. Finally `hpts_aj` states that for all points $x, s$ of $M\eta.C$ over the base with $s$ equal to $\varepsilon$ in the above sense, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to $\mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(x)) - \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(s))$ with `gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)` given by $x$ followed by $\overline{aj}$.
--
--   *The place and the comparison morphisms.* $Pl$ is a valuation subring of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with `Pl.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, $p$ lies in the non-units of $Pl$; $\rho : A \to Pl$ is a ring homomorphism inducing the structure map $A \to \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ (`hρ`), and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ is a surjective ring homomorphism with $\rho$ followed by $\pi_k$ the structure map $A \to k$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`). $P$ and $P'$ are two $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$-points of $M\eta.C$ over the base. The morphisms $j\eta$ and $j_k$ go from $X_{\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}}$, respectively $X_k$, to $X_{Pl} = X\times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} Pl$, and are required to commute with the first projections (`hjη₁`, `hjk₁`) and, on the second projections, with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ and of $\pi_k$ respectively (`hjη₂`, `hjk₂`).
--
--   *The line bundle.* $M_b$ is a module on $X_{Pl}$ which is invertible in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible` (`hL`), and whose pullback along $j\eta$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` at $P'$ tensored with the ideal module of `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` at $P$ — both points transported to $X_{\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}}$ via $e\eta$ and the first projection — that is, $\mathcal{O}(P')\otimes\mathcal{O}(P)^{-1}$ (`hgen`); moreover the pullbacks of $M_b$ along $i_1$ followed by $j_k$ and along $i_2$ followed by $j_k$ are isomorphic to the unit modules of $C_1$ and $C_2$ (`hcomp₁`, `hcomp₂`). Finally $D_v$ is a degree-zero divisor of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ equal to $\mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(P')) - \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(P))$, the places being those attached by `Mη.pointEquivPlace` (`hDv`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist a point $z$ of `D.toBase` over $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho) : \operatorname{Spec} Pl \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and an element $y$ of $G.J_{0s}$ such that: first, the $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$-point `gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)` of $D$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ followed by $z$; second, the $k$-point `pts y` of the base of `D.baseChange k`, followed by the first projection `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A k)` to $D.P$, equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $z$; and third, $\mathrm{proj}\, y = 0$, so that $y$ lies in the subgroup `torus`, the kernel of $\mathrm{proj}$.
--
--   This is the step, in the study of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ and of its special fibre at $p$, which converts a line bundle on the model over a valuation ring $Pl \mid p$ — with generic fibre $\mathcal{O}(P')\otimes\mathcal{O}(P)^{-1}$ and trivial restriction to each of the two components of the geometric special fibre — into an extension of the class $[P']-[P]$ to a $Pl$-point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ whose specialisation lies in the toric part of the special fibre group. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_points_valuationSubring_and_proj_eq_zero_pic0Mk_single_sub_single_of_mem_inertia_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_points_valuationSubring_and_proj_eq_zero_pic0Mk_single_sub_single_of_mem_inertia_of_curveModel_igusa_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and is proved from the two companion statements producing, respectively, the rigidified Poincaré description of the class and the vanishing of its projection.
